`bump` writes memory its caller can see at 
reject_thread_task_shared_write.ts:10:3, and `spawn`
` runs it beside the scope's other tasks: make scratch only this task uses inside it, because an object handed in as the argument is shared memory even when the `spawn` made it, since where an argument was made is not tracked. Write memory the tasks share only through the guard of a `Mutex`; hand a value the parent needs back as the task's answer, or run it on the thread that called it, `out[0] = bump(c)`
